From c06db5156d9953bc0f24a5c9bb8d10fee7b65d6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Nov 2025 10:47:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Writing Claims feature for students with exceptionalities

Implement comprehensive guided claim construction system to help students
with ADHD, dyslexia, ADD, SLD, SLI, and autism build strong writing claims
through progressive scaffolding and AI-powered support.

Key Features:
- Progressive scaffolding with 3 support levels (MINIMAL, MODERATE, MAXIMUM)
- AI-generated probing questions adapted to topic and subject
- Context-aware sentence starters to reduce cognitive load
- Dynamic sentence frames with fill-in-the-blank templates
- Topic-agnostic design works for any subject
- Celebration system for positive reinforcement
- Accessibility-first design principles

Database Changes:
- Add WritingClaim, ClaimStep, and SentenceFrame models
- Add SupportLevel, ClaimStatus, and StepType enums
- Add writingSupportLevel preference to UserPreferences

API Endpoints:
- POST   /api/writing-claims - Create new claim with AI probes
- GET    /api/writing-claims - List all claims
- GET    /api/writing-claims/:id - Get specific claim
- PATCH  /api/writing-claims/:id/steps/:stepId - Submit step response
- POST   /api/writing-claims/:id/generate-frame - Generate sentence frames
- PATCH  /api/writing-claims/:id/complete - Complete claim
- PATCH  /api/writing-claims/:id/archive - Archive claim
- DELETE /api/writing-claims/:id - Delete claim
- GET    /api/writing-claims/:id/hint - Get accessibility hints

Implementation:
- WritingClaimService: AI-powered guidance with Claude integration
- WritingClaimController: RESTful endpoints with Zod validation
- Comprehensive API documentation with examples
